6 = 0(2)\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{blue}(2)$, we can solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 2x - 4y - 6 &= 0 \\\\ 2x - 4y &= 6 \\\\ 2x &= 6 + 4y \\\\ x &= \\dfrac{6 + 4y}{2} \\\\ x &= 3 + 2y \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=3+2y$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$ and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 6x - 8y - 31 &= 0 \\\\ 6(3 + 2y) - 8y - 31 &= 0 \\\\ 18 + 12y - 8y - 31 &= 0 \\\\ -13 + 4y &= 0 \\\\ 4y &= 13 \\\\ y &= \\dfrac{13}{4} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{13}{4}\n$$\n\ninto equation $\\color{red}(1)$, then we can find the value of $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 6x - 8y - 31 &= 0 \\\\ 6x - 8\\left(\\dfrac{13}{4}\\right) - 31 &= 0 \\\\ 6x - 26 - 31 &= 0 \\\\ 6x - 57 &= 0 \\\\ 6x &= 57 \\\\ x &= \\dfrac{19}{2} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=\\dfrac{19}{2}$ and\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{13}{4}\n$$\n\n, which can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac{19}{2},\\dfrac{13}{4}\\right)\n$$" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505002 1068 #edb/ref 17592186505024 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505002 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505002 1071 "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$\\{7a - 8b + 41 = 0; 4a - 4b + 20 = 0$" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505002 1072 #uuid "037d812f-9cb8-5f58-959c-05369edfd299" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505002 1074 "Sometimes, it's handy to assign a number to each equation in a system, so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\{7a - 8b + 41 = 0(1); 4a - 4b + 20 = 0(2)\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{blue}(2)$, we can solve for $a$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 4a - 4b + 20 &= 0 \\\\ 4a - 4b &= -20 \\\\ 4a &= -20 + 4b \\\\ a &= \\dfrac{-20 + 4b}{4} \\\\ a &= -5 + b \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $a=-5+b$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$ and solve for $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 7a - 8b + 41 &= 0 \\\\ 7(-5 + b) - 8b + 41 &= 0 \\\\ -35 + 7b - 8b + 41 &= 0 \\\\ 6 - b &= 0 \\\\ -b &= -6 \\\\ b &= 6 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute\n\n$$\nb=6\n$$\n\ninto equation $\\color{red}(1)$, then we can find the value of $a$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 7a - 8b + 41 &= 0 \\\\ 7a - 8\\left(6\\right) + 41 &= 0 \\\\ 7a - 48 + 41 &= 0 \\\\ 7a - 7 &= 0 \\\\ 7a &= 7 \\\\ a &= 1 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=1$ and\n\n$$\nb=6\n$$\n\n, which can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left(1,6\\right)\n$$" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505003 1080 "-1" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505003 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505003 1083 #uuid "05d9c1d8-7776-59ee-ab3f-0c7ec5d99ad7" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505004 1068 #edb/ref 17592186505088 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505004 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505004 1071 "Using the method of substitution, find the solution of\n$\\{2x + y = -7; 2x - 3y = 13$." 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505004 1072 #uuid "0b3f4cbe-31b3-5a2d-8c6e-81aafdba130b" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505004 1074 "Sometimes, it's handy to assign a number to each equation in a system, so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\{2x + y + 7 = 0(1); 2x - 3y - 13 = 0(2)\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{blue}(1)$, we can solve for $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} y + 2x + 7 &= 0 \\\\ y + 2x &= -7 \\\\ y &= -7 - 2x \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y=-7-2x$ into equation $\\color{red}(2)$ and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -3y + 2x - 13 &= 0 \\\\ -3(-7 - 2x) + 2x - 13 &= 0 \\\\ 21 + 6x + 2x - 13 &= 0 \\\\ 8 + 8x &= 0 \\\\ 8x &= -8 \\\\ x &= -1 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute\n\n$$\nx=-1\n$$\n\ninto equation $\\color{red}(2)$, then we can find the value of $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -3y + 2x - 13 &= 0 \\\\ -3y + 2\\left(-1\\right) - 13 &= 0 \\\\ -3y - 2 - 13 &= 0 \\\\ -3y - 15 &= 0 \\\\ -3y &= 15 \\\\ y &= -5 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $y=-5$ and\n\n$$\nx=-1\n$$\n\n, which can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left(-1,-5\\right)\n$$" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505005 1068 #edb/ref 17592186505034 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505005 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505005 1071 "Using the method of substitution, find the solution of\n\n$\\{-6p - 9q = -6; 3p + 3q = 6$" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505005 1072 #uuid "0bd6815d-c6b1-5fc3-bc01-5728aba3b215" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505005 1074 "Sometimes, it's handy to assign a number to each equation in a system, so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\{-6p - 9q + 6 = 0(1); 3p + 3q - 6 = 0(2)\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{blue}(2)$, we can solve for $q$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 3q + 3p - 6 &= 0 \\\\ 3q + 3p &= 6 \\\\ 3q &= 6 - 3p \\\\ q &= \\dfrac{6 - 3p}{3} \\\\ q &= 2 - p \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $q=2-p$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$ and solve for $p$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -9q - 6p + 6 &= 0 \\\\ -9(2 - p) - 6p + 6 &= 0 \\\\ -18 + 9p - 6p + 6 &= 0 \\\\ -12 + 3p &= 0 \\\\ 3p &= 12 \\\\ p &= 4 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute\n\n$$\np=4\n$$\n\ninto equation $\\color{red}(1)$, then we can find the value of $q$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -9q - 6p + 6 &= 0 \\\\ -9q - 6\\left(4\\right) + 6 &= 0 \\\\ -9q - 24 + 6 &= 0 \\\\ -9q - 18 &= 0 \\\\ -9q &= 18 \\\\ q &= -2 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $q=-2$ and\n\n$$\np=4\n$$\n\n, which can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left(4,-2\\right)\n$$" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505006 1080 "x = -2, y = 8" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505006 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505006 1083 #uuid "0f226940-943f-583c-bfad-7e0e457a4495" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505007 1080 "p = 61, q = -32" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505007 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505007 1083 #uuid "0f359dcf-82e1-573f-b829-c73044894a0a" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505008 1075 #edb/ref 17592186505069 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505008 1075 #edb/ref 17592186505077 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505008 1075 #edb/ref 17592186505078 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505008 1075 #edb/ref 17592186505082 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505008 1075 #edb/ref 17592186505086 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505008 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505008 1077 "selection" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505008 1078 #edb/ref 17592186505078 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505008 1079 #uuid "0f45a298-4422-5551-8d83-c2422dc2c4cd" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505009 1080 "x = \\dfrac{13}{4}, y = \\dfrac{19}{2}" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505009 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505009 1083 #uuid "0f73540b-32d9-5ee1-94a3-da5422f97d77" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505010 1080 "x = \\dfrac{13}{3}, y = -\\dfrac{7}{3}" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505010 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505010 1083 #uuid "1603d82b-c052-55fd-9a55-a364ff5e2cfc" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [