igned} 2x - 4y - 6 &= 0 \\\\ 2x - 4y &= 6 \\\\ 2x &= 6 + 4y \\\\ x &= \\dfrac{6 + 4y}{2} \\\\ x &= 3 + 2y \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=3+2y$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$ and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 7x - 7y - 35 &= 0 \\\\ 7(3 + 2y) - 7y - 35 &= 0 \\\\ 21 + 14y - 7y - 35 &= 0 \\\\ -14 + 7y &= 0 \\\\ 7y &= 14 \\\\ y &= 2 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute\n\n$$\ny=2\n$$\n\ninto equation $\\color{red}(1)$, then we can find the value of $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 7x - 7y - 35 &= 0 \\\\ 7x - 7\\left(2\\right) - 35 &= 0 \\\\ 7x - 14 - 35 &= 0 \\\\ 7x - 49 &= 0 \\\\ 7x &= 49 \\\\ x &= 7 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=7$ and\n\n$$\ny=2\n$$\n\n, which can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left(7,2\\right)\n$$" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505081 1068 #edb/ref 17592186505035 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505081 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505081 1071 "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$\\{4b + 32 = 0; 5a + 2b - 19 = 0$" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505081 1072 #uuid "e7e74981-78de-5721-8c70-6b15d18904de" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505081 1074 "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{red}(1)$, we can solve for $b$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 4b + 32 &= 0 \\\\ 4b &= -32 \\\\ b &= -8 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=-8$ into equation $\\color{blue}(2)$ and solve for $a$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 5a + 2b - 19 &= 0 \\\\ 5a + 2\\left(-8\\right) - 19 &= 0 \\\\ 5a - 16 - 19 &= 0 \\\\ 5a &= 35 \\\\ a &= 7 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a - b = 7 - \\left(-8\\right) = 15$." 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505082 1080 "p = 47, q = -50" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505082 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505082 1083 #uuid "eae0b3dd-9a86-5ad5-b884-59fe84fe608a" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505083 1080 "x = 13, y = -11" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505083 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505083 1083 #uuid "eb4cd44a-762e-558f-bf0a-b46105f41178" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505084 1068 #edb/ref 17592186505056 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505084 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505084 1071 "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$\\{-10x - 10y + 7 = 0; 4x + 8y - 16 = 0$" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505084 1072 #uuid "ed97dc9b-b6f4-5076-b3bb-6acac17b72a7" 13194139535454 17592186045443 true] [17592186505084 1074 "Sometimes, it's handy to assign a number to each equation in a system, so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\{-10x - 10y + 7 = 0(1); 4x + 8y - 16 = 0(2)\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{blue}(2)$, we can solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 4x + 8y - 16 &= 0 \\\\ 4x + 8y &= 16 \\\\ 4x &= 16 - 8y \\\\ x &= \\dfrac{16 - 8y}{4} \\\\ x &= 4 - 2y \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=4-2y$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$ and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -10x - 10y + 7 &= 0 \\\\ -10(4 - 2y) - 10y + 7 &= 0 \\\\ -40 + 20y - 10y + 7 &= 0 \\\\ -33 + 10y &= 0 \\\\ 10y &= 33 \\\\ y &= \\dfrac{33}{10} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{33}{10}\n$$\n\ninto equation $\\color{red}(1)$, then we can find the value of $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -10x - 10y + 7 &= 0 \\\\ -10x - 10\\left(\\dfrac{33}{10}\\right) + 7 &= 0 \\\\ -10x - 33 + 7 &= 0 \\\\ -10x - 26 &= 0 \\\\ -10x &= 26 \\\\ x &= -\\dfrac{13}{5} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-\\dfrac{13}{5}$ and\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{33}{10}\n$$\n\n, which can